{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSet"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Looped vertices are removed and each connected component solved alone, since the rule","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"composes across components. A bipartite component costs O(m √n), as in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"maximumIndependentSet()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", whose core pass in index order already gives the least set. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"complete component takes its least vertex. Any other component of c vertices is decided","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex by vertex in index order against a witness maximum set, shrunk between decisions by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rules that keep the least set (an isolated vertex is taken; so is a simplicial vertex, such","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as a leaf, less than all its neighbours), with pieces that turn bipartite or complete handed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to the cases above. Each decision the witness cannot answer is one solve of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"maximumIndependentSet()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"‘s kind on what is left of the vertex’s component. So trees with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"few extra edges, long paths and cycles cost O(c (c + m)) at worst and O(c + m) when the rules","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"settle them, but a component the rules do not settle can cost up to c exponential searches,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"far more than ","type":"text"},{"code":"maximumIndependentSet()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Memory O(n + m + k² \/ 64) words for a kernel","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"component of k vertices. The search does not check for task cancellation.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The lexicographically first maximum independent set: of all the largest ones, the least by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex index, in "},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" order; [] for the empty graph. Of two sets of one size, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lesser holds the least vertex of their symmetric difference (the rule of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumClique()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so on a loop-free graph this is that clique of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"complement). A vertex with a self-loop is never in it; parallel edges count once."}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"],"name":"Covering"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Method","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P8CoveringE43lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSetSay6VertexQzGyF","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"method","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Covering\/ExactCovering.swift#L1694","fileName":"ExactCovering.swift"},"title":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSet()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSet"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering","doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/lexicographicallyfirstmaximumindependentset()"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSet()"},"references":{"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering":{"url":"\/documentation\/covering","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"Covering","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph/lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSet()":{"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSet"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The lexicographically first maximum independent set: of all the largest ones, the least by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex index, in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order; [] for the empty graph. Of two sets of one size, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"lesser holds the least vertex of their symmetric difference (the rule of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumClique()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so on a loop-free graph this is that clique of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"complement). A vertex with a self-loop is never in it; parallel edges count once.","type":"text"}],"title":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSet()","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSet()","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/lexicographicallyfirstmaximumindependentset()"},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"fragments":[{"text":"extension","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph","title":"Graph","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Graph/Vertex":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"associatedtype"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","text":"Hashable"}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/graph\/vertex","type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"Vertex","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols":{"type":"topic","abstract":[],"role":"collection","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols","title":"GraphProtocols"}}}